    rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) spicule rays as Plateau borders of the secreting cell field vs Grantia ray angles (Pass 2: null control, sweep closure, ablations, three samples) — Code-to-model traceability: 78/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-28"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Header now states P1-P3, E1-E9, F1-F4 and the ablations with page numbers; each analysis function names its prediction (F1 saturation, F2 null, F4 ordering); the Lean header and KG yaml map theorems to equations and functions. Deductions: KG code loci are by function name; segmentation constants (90/400/1500/0.9; population 0.06/5-26 px; drawing 0.10) are tuned to these images and traced only to the plate." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-024-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-024-code-traceability-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 7.8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-024-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) spicule rays as Plateau borders of the secreting cell field vs Grantia ray angles (Pass 2: null control, sweep closure, ablations, three samples) — Model fidelity to source: 78/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-28"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Everything Thompson states algebraically is implemented exactly and Lean-checked, and v2 adds the law-of-sines inverse, the saturation demonstration (F1) and the explicit falsifiable-content statement, which is the honest reading of a tension-triangle model. Still no foam / cell-doublet simulation of the deposition field itself (the GIF's three-cell field remains illustrative), and ray curvature is treated as a measurement nuisance rather than modelled (Thompson's own 'bourrelet' remark)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "thompson/claims/t1917-024_on-concretions-spicules-and-spicular-skeletons.py L557–L564: three_cell_field: cells on sector bisectors, not a tension-derived foam <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/94f2bb26b6ace7b3ff6e099ae0c8472784d36c7c/thompson/claims/t1917-024_on-concretions-spicules-and-spicular-skeletons.py#L557-L564>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-024-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-024-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-024-model-fidelity-3> ;
    pk:hasScore 7.8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-024-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) spicule rays as Plateau borders of the secreting cell field vs Grantia ray angles (Pass 2: null control, sweep closure, ablations, three samples) — Morphometric validation: 76/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-28"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The tautological Pass-1 angle plane is replaced by a real test: closest-pair difference vs a stated null (Dirichlet partition), per spicule and as a set (MC p with resolution floor, KS), with the method's own noise floor measured on known renders; alternatives scored on the same data (RMSE/AIC); P1 tested on an independent population sample with its own null; Thompson's own figure digitised and tested; near- vs chord-axis sensitivity, angle CV and within-type rho CV reported. Deductions: n = 8 + 25 + 4 from three heterogeneous sources; the population method accepts only 28 of 273 junction candidates (selection effects unquantified); the AIC treats the lattice snap as 0 free parameters (generous to the alternative, but a discrete-choice penalty is debatable); projection error of trihedral spicules is bounded only indirectly (near vs chord RMSE 5.3 deg)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-024/measurements/population_ray_angles.json (generated output, not in repo): 28 detections from 273 junction candidates: strong selection, unquantified — datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-024/measurements/population_ray_angles.json: rendered output of thompson/claims/t1917-024_on-concretions-spicules-and-spicular-skeletons.py at 94f2bb26b6ace7b3ff6e099ae0c8472784d36c7c, application/json, 18394 B, artifact_sha256 d3c866f029dc228b4f6302bd194be595d49cb02f741e34f10cd652b498a69bb5 (sha256 d3c866f029dc228b4f6302bd194be595d49cb02f741e34f10cd652b498a69bb5), spec_fingerprint 77e8201d27dd51cb520268fe921b47c6a9cc21b65c7f28e750eaa978978c6f12" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-024-measurement-alternative-model-rmse-crystal-120-0-params>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-024-measurement-closest-pair-angle-difference-d-median-sem>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-024-measurement-fitted-rho-cv-within-tubar-triactines-panel-d-n-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-024-measurement-near-axis-vs-chord-axis-angle-sensitivity-pearson-r>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-024-measurement-population-micrograph-mean-theta-120-over-physical-triradiates>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-024-measurement-rho-sweep-measurement-closure-pearson-r-true-vs-re-measured-theta-pair>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-024-measurement-tetrahedral-inter-ray-angle-e7>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-024-measurement-thompson-fig-214-digitised-closest-pair-difference-d-median>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-024-measurement-three-ray-spicules-measured-on-the-sem-plate>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-024-measurement-unpaired-angle-deviation-from-the-paired-angle-mean-sem>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-024-morphometric-validation-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-024-morphometric-validation-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-024-morphometric-validation-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-024-morphometric-validation-4> ;
    pk:hasScore 7.6e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-024-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) spicule rays as Plateau borders of the secreting cell field vs Grantia ray angles (Pass 2: null control, sweep closure, ablations, three samples) — MorphoEval overall 75.9/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-28"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "TESTED CLAIM, verdict MIXED. Model: Neumann tension triangle E1-E3 with the equiangular point E4, one-parameter sagittal family E5 (cos theta_pair = -rho/2), tetrahedral / orthogonal limits E7/E8 and the law-of-sines inverse; six Lean theorems; the general three-tension model is shown saturated (realises 100 % of random angle triplets) so only E5 is tested. Measurement: PCA ray axes from radial arcs, validated by rendering 20 E5 spicules at known rho in random orientation and re-measuring (r = 0.9999, RMSE 0.35 deg, rho RMSE 0.011, d noise floor <= 2.3 deg). SEM plate (8 three-ray spicules): closest-pair difference d median 4.4 deg vs Dirichlet null median 34.8 (set-mean MC p < 5e-5, KS p = 8e-6, 5/8 below the null 5th percentile); unpaired deviation 26 deg; fitted rho 0.20 (T- shaped atrial tetractine f) to 1.12; all 7 spicules with rho < 1 have unpaired > paired (F4); rho CV within the three tubar triactines d = 0.004. Alternatives on the same angles: crystal-120 RMSE 15.3, lattice-30 8.5, E5 2.25 deg (E5 preferred by AIC). Population spread (25 physical triradiates of 28 detections): mean |theta - 120| = 17.3 vs null 71.2; all-within-15 fraction 0.52 vs null 0.011 (P1). Thompson's own Fig. 214 panels A-D digitised: 92/108/160, 89/93/178, 110/110/140, 115/121/125; d median 3.5, set-mean MC p = 0.0012; E and F unresolved (hairline drawings). Not tested: P3 (tetrahedral; apical ray end-on in 2D), alcyonarian spicules, and the mechanism itself, which modern sclerocyte biology contradicts in Thompson's 'any three cells' form. Rubric scores rate the simulation package. Overall 75.9/100. Overall 75.9/100 (faithfulness 74.7, reproducibility 78.7); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 94f2bb26b6ace7b3ff6e099ae0c8472784d36c7c; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 78, Morphological realism / specimen match 70, Parameter expressivity 78, Morphometric validation 76, Source and data traceability 85, Code-to-model traceability 78, Reproducibility package 74. Output judged: docs/media/t1917_024_on_concretions_spicules_and_sp_comparison.png: rendered output of thompson/claims/t1917-024_on-concretions-spicules-and-spicular-skeletons.py at 94f2bb26b6ace7b3ff6e099ae0c8472784d36c7c, image/png, 587937 B, 1900×1250 px, artifact_sha256 e4526bfdf295d88731e41f15187b4f2dee07e46d148a0f2b39d42425edfa6985 (sha256 e4526bfdf295d88731e41f15187b4f2dee07e46d148a0f2b39d42425edfa6985), spec_fingerprint 77e8201d27dd51cb520268fe921b47c6a9cc21b65c7f28e750eaa978978c6f12. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 77e8201d27dd51cb520268fe921b47c6a9cc21b65c7f28e750eaa978978c6f12; artifact_sha256: e4526bfdf295d88731e41f15187b4f2dee07e46d148a0f2b39d42425edfa6985; input_dataset_sha256: {dryad_8mv00jv_dataset_metadata.json=8b1273b453ccdb77..., grantia_indica_zootaxa4426_fig53_sem.jpg=70194abe78894820..., grantia_spicules_readey_100x.jpg=08641621770534e1..., thompson1917_fig214_ia_leaf465_p445.jpg=019168c1fa4adddc...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-28-t1917-024-on-concretions-spicules-and-sp-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Thompson (1917, pp. 443-449), after Dreyer (1892) and Plateau (1873): calcareous spicule rays follow the junction lines of 3 or 4 contiguous cells; 120 deg for equal tensions, 'two equal angles and one unequal' otherwise, grading to a T; tetrahedral ~109 deg for four cells; the spicule is 'a crystal under restraint'. Evidence given: Haeckel's drawings (Fig. 214), no angle table.; reconstructed_in_script: Exact Neumann law of cosines / law of sines, E5 family and inverse, tetrahedral and orthogonal constants, interstice area; PCA radial-arc ray-angle extraction validated by a rendered rho sweep; Dirichlet(1,1,1) null for the closest-pair difference with MC and KS tests; crystal-120 and lattice-30 ablations with RMSE/AIC; three samples (CC BY SEM plate n = 8, CC BY-SA population spread n = 25 physical, Thompson Fig. 214 n = 4 panels); result.json with per-prediction verdict components.; transfer_boundary: One SEM plate from one individual and one spread of one Grantia sample; drawings are Haeckel's not photographs; 2D projections of trihedral spicules (near- vs chord-axis RMSE 5.3 deg quantifies curvature/projection sensitivity); no alcyonarian material; tetractine apical ray not measurable.; does_not_claim: Does NOT claim Thompson's mechanism is correct: Ledger & Jones (1977) and Voigt et al. (2017) show a dedicated founder/thickener sclerocyte sextet; only the geometric predictions are supported, and bilateral symmetry of that sextet would also yield two equal angles — the data cannot separate tension balance from a symmetric cell programme. | Does NOT claim the general three-tension model is tested: it is saturated (fraction realised 1.0) and cannot fail; only E5 is falsifiable here. | Does NOT claim P3 (tetrahedral 109.47 deg) or anything about alcyonarian spicules; both are 'untestable' in result.json. | Does NOT use the pre-assigned Dryad dataset (hexactine fossil tomograms, 5.8 GB): DATASET_MISMATCH recorded with pinned metadata. | Does NOT claim independent confirmation: builder-scored (R1 open).." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: {'id': 'R1', 'item': 'Independent second assessor (different provider) — Pass 2 is still builder-scored'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R10', 'item': 'Quantify population-extraction selection: manually annotate a random subset of the 273 junction candidates to estimate the acceptance bias of the 3-arc criterion'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R11', 'item': 'Model ray curvature (Plateau bourrelet / curved partitions of unequal cells) so the near- vs chord-axis difference (RMSE 5.3 deg) becomes a prediction, not a nuisance'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R12', 'item': '3D test of P3: micro-CT or stereo-SEM of tetractines to measure the apical ray angle against 109.47 deg'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R13', 'item': 'Alcyonarian (octocoral) sclerites: the claim text names them and nothing here tests them'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R9', 'item': 'A second SEM individual/species (e.g. Sycon, Leucosolenia plates in Zootaxa 4426 or other CC BY sources) so the SEM d-statistic is not n = 8 from one specimen'}" ;
    pk:hasScore 7.59e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

